// monitors.example.zon — the display layout, split out of config.zon.
//
// This file is a REFERENCE and a test fixture; unlike config.example.zon it is
// deliberately NOT installed to /etc, because a system-wide monitor layout would
// be found by every user who has no monitors.zon of their own and would rotate or
// reposition their screens on the strength of an example.
//
// One file, one layout. To keep several (docked, undocked, a desktop), keep a
// file per arrangement and make `monitors.zon` a SYMLINK to the one in use:
//
//     ~/.config/reach/monitors.zon -> monitors/docked.zon
//
// Re-pointing the link and reloading (Super+Shift+r, or `kill -HUP $(pidof reach)`)
// is then the whole docking gesture. reach knows nothing about that arrangement:
// it opens `monitors.zon`, the kernel follows the link, and the layout is
// re-applied only if it actually CHANGED by value — so a reload that switches
// nothing costs no flicker, and a dangling link reads as no file at all.
//
// Every field except `name` is optional and falls back to the same default a
// `.monitors` entry in config.zon has.
.{
    // Array ORDER is monitor numbering: it decides focusmon/tagmon direction and
    // the `.monitor` index window rules in config.zon use. A head that is not
    // connected is simply ignored, so a layout may list more than is plugged in.
    .monitors = .{
        // Always give an explicit .x/.y. The defaults are -1,-1, which means
        // "don't send set_position" — the compositor then auto-places the head
        // wherever it likes, which is how a rotated panel ends up beside its
        // neighbour instead of above it.
        .{ .name = "DP-5", .w = 1920, .h = 1080, .x = 0, .y = 0 },
        .{ .name = "eDP-1", .w = 1920, .h = 1200, .x = 0, .y = 1080 },
        // A rotated head's .w/.h are its MODE; the transform swaps them on the
        // desktop. This one is 1920x1080 here and occupies 1080x1920, so a
        // neighbour to its right would start at .x = 1920 + 1080.
        .{ .name = "DP-3", .w = 1920, .h = 1080, .x = 1920, .y = 0, .transform = .rotate_270 },
    },
}
